Language.String:
Real Glass: the glass each building asset has of its own, on every copy of it, in every city. Nothing of it is kept in your saves.

 One Asset element per asset, holding only what it does not take from RealGlass.xml, under the same names and in the same units:
 - a percentage the way its slider shows it: 47 means 47%; GlassThreshold goes from 10 to 95 (lower than in RealGlass.xml: it is this asset's alone);
 - GlassColor as #RRGGBB; GlassNightWindows as true or false;
 - GlassPreset as the number of a kind of glass (0 Custom, 1 to 10, as in RealGlass.xml); a kind of glass alone gives its colour, reflectivity and clarity.

 The F8 panel's Asset tab writes this file (pick a building with the picker key). You can edit it while the game is running too: the mod reads it again within a second. Take an asset's element out, or delete the file with the game closed, and it has the global glass again.
